  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122436,
      "SummaryText": "Colonial Chemical, Inc., located in rural Marion County, TN, is a leader in the manufacture of surfactant products based on renewable ingredients. Colonial is committed to producing safe products while protecting the health and safety of its employees and the surrounding community.\n\nColonial receives epichlorohydrin\u0097derived from plant-based glycerol\u0097in bulk containers. The epichlorohydrin is transferred from these containers to a closed atmospheric storage tank equipped with a full vapor recovery system to prevent the release of vapors.\n\nSafety systems for epichlorohydrin include multiple layers of overfill and overpressure prevention, nitrogen inerting, remote emergency shutdown and isolation devices, interlocks and alarms, spill containment structures, and an automatic foam deluge system. In the event of a spill, epichlorohydrin can be remotely isolated and blanketed with aqueous fire-fighting foam to suppress toxic vapor emissions and reduce fire risk. All piping that carries epichlorohydrin is fully contained within secondary containment.\n\nOff-site consequence analysis for the hypothetical worst-case scenario involving epichlorohydrin indicates that the potential effects are limited to a small localized rural area adjacent to the Colonial Chemical facility.  Analysis of more realistic scenarios involving failure of unloading or transfer equipment shows that no hazardous exposure is expected outside of the Colonial Chemical facility. \n\nThe robust design and safety features in the epichlorohydrin system, resulting from thorough process hazard analysis and application of industry best practices, along with well-trained and engaged employees has resulted in the safe operation of the process with no accidental releases of epichlorohydrin since startup in 2015."
    }
  ]
